      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, \"goblins\"? I didn't ask for a fantasy story or for you to use creatures like goblins to describe the bacteria. I asked for a dramatic and vivid description for a training manual, but I wanted it to be about the actual biology and the physical reality of the microbes.\n\nCan we try this again? Please rewrite the description to be just as intense and high-stakes, but remove all the references to goblins, armies, or fantasy elements. Focus instead on the microscopic reality—the armored spore coat, the sudden rehydration, and the rapid, invisible takeover of the food. I need the staff to take the science seriously, not feel like they're reading a storybook.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
